cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the associated article and this software version."
title: "Multivariate graph-cut combination of climate models: code and compact results"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Schmutz
    given-names: Lucas
    affiliation: "University of Lausanne, Switzerland"
repository-code: "https://github.com/schmutzlucas/multivariate-graphcut-climate"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - climate-model ensembles
  - multivariate distributions
  - Hellinger distance
  - graph cuts
  - CMIP6
  - ERA5
abstract: >-
  Code, compact numerical results and documentation for "Beyond mean fields:
  a multivariate graph-cut approach to climate-model combination". Regenerates
  all article figures and tables from included results, demonstrates the
  longitude-periodic graph-cut solver, and provides entry points for the full
  ERA5 and perfect-model experiments, which require external prepared
  ERA5/CMIP6 data. Code is MIT-licensed; results, figures and documentation
  are CC BY 4.0. The external graph-cut solver and climate data keep their
  own terms.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Beyond mean fields: a multivariate graph-cut approach to climate-model combination"
    authors:
      - family-names: Schmutz
        given-names: Lucas
    journal: "Earth System Dynamics (manuscript in preparation)"
